# MToon material classes

Grammar: `{Identity}-{Class}.{Class}` — identity uses `_` only; `.` only after `-`.

Examples: `Face_Skin`, `Face_Skin-NoRim.NoOutline`, `Glow-EmissionAccent.NoOutline`, `Iris_Eye-MatcapTexture.NoOutline.NoRim`.

Invalid: `Face.Skin`, `Glow.NoRim` (migrate first). `Glow` is an identity, not a class.

## Theme

Edit workspace [`mtoon_theme.json`](../../mtoon_theme.json). Apply to the **open** `.blend` (incrementals share this file). MCP must pass absolute `theme_path`.

Do not hand-set rim/outline/emission/matcap sockets when a theme compile will do it.

## Classes

| Token | Compile |
|-------|---------|
| `NoRim` | **Parametric Rim Color = black**; **Parametric Rim Lift = 0**; **Parametric Rim Fresnel Power = 1000** |
| `NoOutline` | Skip Outline Width Mode (leave `0`). Still stamp Outline Width + Color |
| `Highlight` | Opt-in theme matcap: `mtoon_matcap_highlight` + factor white |
| `MatcapTexture` | Keep linked MatCap Texture; factor white (not both with `Highlight`) |
| `EmissionAccent` | Lit + Shade + Emissive = `accent` |
| `InvertEmissionAccent` | Lit + Shade + Emissive = `invertAccent` (not both with `EmissionAccent`) |
| `EmissionTexture` | Keep Emissive Texture; **Emissive Factor white**; **Emissive Strength = 1** (not with other Emission* classes) |

Default (no class): rim = accent + theme lift; hide matcap (`mtoon_none_white` + black factor); emission black; lit/shade untouched.

## Workflow

1. Stamp names (`stamp_mtoon_classes`) — dry-run then apply
2. `audit_mtoon_theme` / `apply_mtoon_theme` from [mtoon-material-sync](../../skills/mtoon-material-sync/SKILL.md)
3. Expr `invertAccent` (was `rimPink`) swaps accent↔invertAccent on rim/lit/shade/emission binds

Dummy images: `mtoon_none_white`, `mtoon_none_black`, `mtoon_matcap_highlight` (from `Swimsuit_Front` / `light_matcap`).
